From: nomorecoolnicknames <unisocofficial@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 08 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libipa: add IMX362/IMX260 sensor helper (reuse IMX258 gain law)

The Meizu M6 Note rear sensor (imx362 driver, physical IMX260) shares the Sony
smartphone-sensor gain law with IMX258. Without a helper the simple-IPA AGC
assumes linear gain and oscillates. Register imx362/imx260 to the IMX258 helper.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp	2026-07-08 02:46:23.008515796 -0500
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp	2026-07-08 02:46:43.812814349 -0500
@@ -566,6 +566,22 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx258", CameraSensorHelperImx258)
 
+/*
+ * Sony IMX362 / IMX260 (Meizu M6 Note rear). Same Sony smartphone-sensor
+ * programming interface as the IMX258: analogue gain law gain = 512/(512-code)
+ * and a 0x40 (10-bit) black-level pedestal. Reuse the IMX258 helper so the
+ * simple-IPA AGC maps gain correctly (otherwise exposure/colour oscillate).
+ */
+class CameraSensorHelperImx362 : public CameraSensorHelperImx258
+{
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx362", CameraSensorHelperImx362)
+
+class CameraSensorHelperImx260 : public CameraSensorHelperImx258
+{
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx260", CameraSensorHelperImx260)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperImx283 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
